    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d648">

                <pb facs="0708" n="698" xml:id="pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">858.248/10–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-08T13:00:00+01:00">October 8, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8487. We have given Foreign Office orally the substance of Department’s 8247,
                    October 7, 7 p.m.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d648-f1"/> When doing so we were told
                    that a message had just been received from the British Minister at Stockholm
                    stating that the Secretary General of the Swedish Foreign Office had informed
                    him that Madame Kollontay already knows of the proposed release of airmen and
                    had been promised that in any release effected 10 Russian internees would be
                    simultaneously released “on account”.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Stockholm and Moscow.</p>
                <p>Our 8372, October 5, 7 p.m. has also been repeated to Moscow and Stockholm.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
